      ],
      "explanation": "For a nonzero base, a negative exponent means taking the reciprocal of the corresponding positive power. Thus\n\\[\n(-2)^{-2}=\\frac{1}{(-2)^2}=\\frac14.\n\\]\nEvaluate this power before subtracting:\n\\[\n2-(-2)^{-2}=2-\\frac14=\\boxed{\\frac74},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
